{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>Let them be seven years of famine.</b> ״יהיו״ is an expression of prayer, for by strict justice there should have been forty-two years of famine in Egypt — just as the seven of the cows and the seven of the ears of grain in the dream, and likewise in the narrative, and likewise the total from Joseph's own account: seven of the cows and seven of the ears of grain — that makes forty-two. And through Joseph's prayer they were reduced to seven. Jacob came and they were reduced to two — that makes forty [that were reduced]. And they were exacted from them in the days of Jeremiah, as it is written: ״והיתה מצרים לשממה ארבעים שנה״."], :book :genesis, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 41, :notes {0 "The note appears to say that of the 42 years of famine decreed, 40 were 'reduced' (נחסרו) through the merits of Joseph and Jacob, leaving only 2 actual years of famine; those 40 were then exacted later in Jeremiah's time. The phrase ונפרעו להם is rendered 'were exacted from them.' The quoted verse is from Ezekiel 29:12."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:06:56.147804327Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}